<title>JAPAN: Japan firms' Jan-March capex up 13.0 pct yr/yr-MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan firms' Jan-March capex up 13.0 pct yr/yr-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese firms increased spending on plant and equipment by 13.0 percent in the January to March quarter of 1997 from the same period the previous year, a survey by the Ministry of Finance (MOF) showed on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The quarterly survey covered 8,983 companies in Japan, excluding financial institutions and insurance firms, capitalised at 10 million yen or more.</p>
<p>Year-on-year changes in corporate capital spending, profits and sales were as follows:</p>
<p>				Jan-March	Oct-Dec	July-Sept</p>
<p>Capital spending	  +13.0	   +10.0	   +8.2</p>
<p> manufacturing	    +13.6	    +6.7	   +6.3</p>
<p> non-manufacturing	+12.7	   +11.5	   +9.2</p>
<p>Current profits	   +18.2	   +15.4	  +12.7</p>
<p> manufacturing	    +22.9	   +18.4	  +15.1</p>
<p> non-manufacturing	+15.1	   +12.6	  +10.8</p>
<p>Sales			  +5.1	    +4.9	   +4.4</p>
<p> manufacturing	     +8.9	    +6.3	   +7.2</p>
<p> non-manufacturing	 +3.7	    +4.3	   +3.4</p>
</text>
